# Normalise line endings in the repository and check out LF on every platform.
#
# This is load-bearing rather than cosmetic. This machine has core.autocrlf=true
# (the Windows default), so without this file a fresh Windows clone checks out
# CRLF while a Linux/Render clone gets LF -- the same commit producing different
# bytes on disk depending on who cloned it. The project asserts that a rebuilt
# index is bit-identical to data/processed/vectors.npy, so "same bytes
# everywhere" is a property the test suite depends on.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artefacts. `text=auto` already detects these correctly, but naming them
# states the intent and prevents a later edit from reclassifying them as text.
data/processed/vectors.npy binary
data/processed/*.bin binary
chroma.sqlite3 binary

# Shell and batch entry points keep native endings. A .bat checked out with LF
# fails on Windows; .sh checked out with CRLF fails on Linux.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.sh  text eol=lf
